WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.935
-Attorney General William Barr

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:05.304
testified in Congress today
after news broke

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:06.772
that Special Counsel
Robert Mueller

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:09.309
complained to Barr about his
description of Mueller's report.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:11.210
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.879
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:15.648 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.784
Let's just remember the public
waited almost two years

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:20.620
for Robert Mueller's
final report.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.422
If you tuned into the news, it's
basically all you heard about.

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:24.957
Everyone wanted to see it.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.759
This thing
was more highly anticipated

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.829
than the last Avengers movie,
and almost as long.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.497
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:34.968
I hope -- I hope my burn doesn't
affect your box office.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.769
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:39.238
Everyone wanted answers to some
basic questions.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.674
What happened in 2016?
What was Trump's involvement?

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.409
And what did he do after
the fact

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.878
to interfere in
the investigation?

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.645
But when the report
was finally delivered,

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:49.348
the first we heard about it
wasn't from Mueller himself,

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:52.218
but from William Barr, Trump's
hand-picked Attorney General.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.453
Barr sent that infamous
4-page letter

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:57.156
summarizing Mueller's
448-page report,

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:58.925
which right off the bat
is impossible.

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:02.795
You can't boil a report
that long down to four pages,

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:03.996
and you shouldn't try.

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:06.032
That's like saying
the Battle of Winterfell

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.867
was about a dude who smoked
too much weed

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.102
and thought he was a bird.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.436
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:12.204
And I don't want to make this
all about Bran,

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:14.507
but, Bran, buddy,
what are your powers

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.442
and when are you going to use
them to be helpful?

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.411
[ Laughter ]
You're like --

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:21.347
[ Cheers and applause ]
Bran...

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.383
I know you can hear me, Bran.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.918
You're like Superman
using his x-ray vision

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:27.453
to heat up a Hot Pocket.

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:28.420
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.989
Do you hear me, Bran?

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.657
Bran. Bran!

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:33.726
Don't do that eye thing!

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.728
[ Dramatic music plays ]
Ugh!

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.263
[ Music stops ]

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.332
I don't know why I bother
with this guy.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.734
Barr's initial letter basically
said there was no collusion

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.936
and that Trump was not guilty
of obstructing justice.

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:45.972
And it was a very successful
PR campaign

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.639
because it shaped the initial
media coverage

00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:49.842
of Mueller's report before
we actually got to see it.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.944
And on top of that,
it allowed Trump to claim

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:54.346
over and over again
that he had been exonerated.

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:57.884
-It was a complete
and total exoneration.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.619
The Mueller report was great.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.320
It could not have been better.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.722
The result was great.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.792
No obstruction. No collusion.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.293
No anything.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.628
Total exoneration.

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:12.331
Complete vindication.

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.100
Everybody waited for
the Mueller report,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.303
then it turns out
that there's no obstruction.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.171
No collusion. No anything.

00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:21.507
I won. No collusion.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.242
No obstruction. I won.

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.211
The finding was very,
very strong.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.479
No collusion. No obstruction.

00:02:27.479 --> 00:02:30.083
No Russia. No nothing.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.884
-Trump went so over the top,

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.087
he literally claimed
there was no Russia.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.221
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.555
[ As Trump ]
The report was very strong.

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:38.591
Mueller said there was
no obstruction, no collusion,

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.959
and the country of Russia,
it doesn't even exist.

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:42.395
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.297
[ Normal voice ] In fact,
Trump went so far in celebrating

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.764
after Barr's letter
that he claimed

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:48.134
Democrats were on life support.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:53.172
-After three years of lies
and smears and slander,

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:57.476
the Russia hoax is finally dead.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:00.880
The collusion delusion is over.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:06.452
And they're on artificial
respirators right now.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.554
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:12.591
They're getting mouth to mouth
resuscitation.

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:14.627
-They need mouth to mouth?

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:15.761
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:17.162
Every time you do a rally,

00:03:17.162 --> 00:03:20.365
you look like a guy who got
locked inside a sauna overnight.

00:03:20.365 --> 00:03:21.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.369
But despite Trump's celebrating,

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:26.339
we now know Barr's initial
letter and press conference

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.240
summarizing Mueller's report
were lies.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.309
First of all, Barr left out
all the evidence

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.178
Mueller gathered about
obstruction of justice

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:35.181
and on top of that, he left out
key parts of sentences

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.882
that he quoted from
Mueller's report.

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:40.019
Here's CNN explaining
one glaring example of that.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:43.556
-Mr. Barr cherry-picked
this line.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.091
-Investigation did not establish

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:48.895
that members of the Trump
campaign conspired

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:51.964
or coordinated with
the Russian government

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.867
in its election interference
activities.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.836
-The context is key.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.238
Mr. Barr ignored the first half
of the line.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:02.141
The investigation also
identified numerous links

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:05.344
between the Russian government
and the Trump campaign.

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:08.881
And this line, "The campaign
expected it would benefit

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:12.150
electorally from information
stolen and released

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.153
through Russian efforts."

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.555
-You can't leave out
part of a sentence like that.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.324
That's a huge difference.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.326
That's the difference
between telling a bartender

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.428
who takes your keys,
"I've had four beers,

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.763
six shots of whiskey,
four line of cocaine,

00:04:24.763 --> 00:04:28.167
ten margaritas,
but I'm good to drive" and...

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.535
"I'm good to drive."

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.603
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.603 --> 00:04:35.074
So we already knew Barr's
initial letter was misleading.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.242
And now we know we're not
the only ones who thought that,

00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:39.112
because another person
who complained about it

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:40.413
was Robert Mueller himself.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.981
-We've got breaking news
at this hour

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.416
that one of the chief criticisms

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.217
of Attorney General William
Barr's summary

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:48.053
of the Mueller report
was made by none other than

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:50.456
the Special Counsel himself,
Robert Mueller.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.858
-Justice Department officials
familiar with the issue

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:56.596
tell NBC News that three days
after Barr released his summary

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:59.164
of Mueller's findings,
the Special Counsel

00:04:59.164 --> 00:05:01.500
in a letter reviewed
by "the Washington Post"

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.003
said Barr's descriptions did not
fully capture the context,

00:05:05.003 --> 00:05:09.241
nature, and substance
of Mueller's 448 page report.

00:05:09.241 --> 00:05:11.510
-Wait. So you're telling me
Donald Trump was lying

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:12.378
when he said this?

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:15.347
-No collusion, no obstruction.

00:05:15.347 --> 00:05:17.349
No Russia. No nothing.

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:18.418
Damn it!

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:20.987
But I already took Russia
out of my map!

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.788
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.991
Also, also...

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.326
[ Applause ]

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.728
...just as a general rule,

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:32.264
you never want to get a letter
from Robert Mueller.

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:34.333
You don't even want to get
a look from Robert Mueller.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:37.236
If I bumped into someone
on the street and I looked up

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.205
and saw that face,
I would need...

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:42.141
-Mouth to mouth resuscitation.

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.909
-So now we know that even
Mueller himself

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:45.578
complained that Barr's letter
was misleading,

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.946
which is shocking, because
Barr was specifically asked

00:05:47.946 --> 00:05:49.715
in a previous congressional
hearing if he knew

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:51.083
how Mueller felt about
his letter

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.418
summarizing Mueller's findings.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:55.021
And Barr told members
of Congress he had no idea.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:58.124
-Reports have emerged recently,
General,

00:05:58.124 --> 00:06:00.492
that members of
the Special Counsel's team

00:06:00.492 --> 00:06:04.163
are frustrated at some level
with the limited information

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:07.933
included in
your March 24th letter,

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:11.137
that it does not adequately
or accurately, necessarily,

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.139
portray the report's findings.

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:16.976
Do you know what they're
referencing with that?

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.177
-No, I don't.

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:20.445
-Did Bob Mueller support
your conclusion?

00:06:20.445 --> 00:06:22.047
-I don't know whether Bob
Mueller

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:23.816
supported my conclusion.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.884
-Yeah, you did.
There was a letter.

00:06:25.884 --> 00:06:27.720
And there's no way you just
forgot about

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.054
a letter from Robert Mueller.

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:31.824
That's like forgetting about
a note on your windshield

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:33.826
that says, "I know
what you did last summer."

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.194
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:37.463
So now we know that the guy
who spent almost two years

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:39.698
putting together
a 448 page report

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:42.534
about a criminal conspiracy to
interfere in the 2016 election

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:44.404
complained that Trump's
hand-picked Attorney General

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:45.938
misled the country
about that report.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.139
That's huge news.

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:48.941
And yet, when they had
the chance to ask Barr

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:50.442
about that news
in a hearing today,

00:06:50.442 --> 00:06:53.212
Republican Senators mostly acted
like it didn't happen.

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:54.513
Like Senator Lindsey Graham.

00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:56.648
Now remember, this guy
is the chairman

00:06:56.648 --> 00:06:58.017
of the Senate
Judiciary Committee

00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:00.485
and he's holding a hearing
with the Attorney General

00:07:00.485 --> 00:07:02.387
of the United States about
the Mueller report.

00:07:02.387 --> 00:07:04.023
So you'd expect

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:06.225
that he'd at least read
the whole thing. Right?

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:08.894
-Here's the Mueller report.

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:12.664
You can read it for yourself.

00:07:12.664 --> 00:07:16.301
It's about
400-and-something pages.

00:07:16.301 --> 00:07:19.271
Can't say I've read it all,
but I've read most of it.

00:07:19.271 --> 00:07:21.040
-What do you mean,
you haven't read it?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.608
That was the assignment!

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:23.942
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.942 --> 00:07:26.112
Are you the guy who shows up
to book club, and says,

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:28.581
[ As Graham ] "I'm real excited
to talk about 'Moby Dick,'

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:31.050
but if we could just avoid
any details

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.286
about what happens to the whale,
that would be great.

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:34.419
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.419 --> 00:07:36.555
I didn't get to any
of the whale parts."

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:37.956
[ Normal voice ]
I know it's long,

00:07:37.956 --> 00:07:39.425
but senators should read
the whole report.

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:41.626
It's possible.
I mean, Elizabeth Warren did it.

00:07:41.626 --> 00:07:44.463
-I was on an airplane yesterday,
and started reading it.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.398
Read it way into the night
last night.

00:07:46.398 --> 00:07:48.434
And I got to the end.

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:49.768
-I'm impressed that she read

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:51.837
a 400-page legal document
on an airplane.

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:54.840
And now you know if you sit
next to Elizabeth Warren

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.443
on a night flight, she gonna
have her light on.

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:58.978
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:02.748
Oh, now time to get some sleep.
Oh, no, Elizabeth Warren!

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:04.149
[ Laughter ]

00:08:04.149 --> 00:08:06.352
So Graham admitted he hadn't
even read the whole report.

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:08.520
And then he decided to spend
the rest of his time

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.323
harping not on Mueller, but on
the GOP's favorite obsession,

00:08:11.323 --> 00:08:13.425
Hillary Clinton.
Specifically he went back

00:08:13.425 --> 00:08:16.094
and read old unearthed texts
from FBI agents

00:08:16.094 --> 00:08:18.330
involved in the Hillary Clinton
e-mail investigation

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.532
to claim that they were
bias against Trump.

00:08:20.532 --> 00:08:23.568
-This is what Strzok said
on February 12th, 2016.

00:08:23.568 --> 00:08:26.238
Now he's in charge of the
Clinton e-mail investigation.

00:08:26.238 --> 00:08:29.442
Oh he's -- Trump's -- abysmal.

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:31.677
I keep hoping the charade
will end

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.645
and people will just dump him.

00:08:33.645 --> 00:08:36.716
February 12th, 2016.

00:08:36.716 --> 00:08:39.918
Page is
the Department of Justice lawyer

00:08:39.918 --> 00:08:41.454
assigned to this case.

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:43.622
March 3rd, 2016.

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:46.392
God, Trump is a loathsome
human being.

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:51.130
Strzok -- Oh, my God.
Trump's an idiot.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.565
Page -- he's awful.

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:54.733
I cannot believe Trump is likely

00:08:54.733 --> 00:08:58.137
to be an actual serious
candidate for president.

00:08:58.137 --> 00:09:00.973
July 21st, 2016.

00:09:00.973 --> 00:09:02.775
Trump is a disaster.

00:09:02.775 --> 00:09:05.043
-I love that Graham think
it's incredible gotcha

00:09:05.043 --> 00:09:07.546
to read a bunch of text messages
from FBI officials

00:09:07.546 --> 00:09:09.782
calling this guy a disaster.
I mean, look at him.

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:11.183
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:13.386
if you saw him on the street
and had no idea who he was,

00:09:13.386 --> 00:09:16.122
you'd say, "Man,
that guy's a disaster."

00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:17.322
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.322 --> 00:09:19.358
But the best part was when
Graham read a text

00:09:19.358 --> 00:09:20.893
that had an expletive in it,

00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:23.061
and maybe didn't realize
that he was being broadcast

00:09:23.061 --> 00:09:24.496
live on cable news.

00:09:24.496 --> 00:09:27.365
October 19th, 2016.

00:09:27.365 --> 00:09:29.335
Trump is a [bleep] idiot.

00:09:29.335 --> 00:09:30.469
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.469 --> 00:09:33.272
He's unable to provide
a coherent answer.

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:34.840
Sorry to the kids out there.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.375
[ Laughter ]

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:38.744
-[ Antebellum accent ]
Why, Lindsey Beauregard Graham,

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:40.312
I do declare!

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:41.647
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:43.783
[ Normal voice ]
Man, you know, it's getting

00:09:43.783 --> 00:09:46.284
so you can't even take your kids
out of school

00:09:46.284 --> 00:09:48.019
on a Wednesday morning

00:09:48.019 --> 00:09:52.224
and watch a congressional
hearing together as a family!

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:53.759
[ Laughter ]

00:09:53.759 --> 00:09:55.861
Graham definitely, definitely --

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:59.932
[ Applause ]

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:02.668
Graham definitely forgot
this thing was being broadcast

00:10:02.668 --> 00:10:03.735
live on cable news.

00:10:03.735 --> 00:10:05.170
He probably assumed

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.472
he was just on C-SPAN,

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:07.940
where you can say and do
whatever you want,

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.709
because nobody is watching.

00:10:09.709 --> 00:10:11.510
I turned it on C-SPAN
the other day

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:14.146
and was just a couple dogs
humping in an empty chamber.

00:10:14.146 --> 00:10:15.380
[ Laughter ]

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.616
People don't know,
C-SPAN is like '90s Cinemax.

00:10:17.616 --> 00:10:18.884
At 3:00 a.m.,
they hold hearings,

00:10:18.884 --> 00:10:20.419
but they're just like
blurred out.

00:10:20.419 --> 00:10:23.555
[ Laughter ]

00:10:23.555 --> 00:10:25.824
But aside from dropping
an F-bomb on live TV,

00:10:25.824 --> 00:10:27.826
Graham also decided
to briefly dabble

00:10:27.826 --> 00:10:28.995
in what was supposed to be
the main point

00:10:28.995 --> 00:10:30.095
of the hearing,
the Mueller report.

00:10:30.095 --> 00:10:31.530
Now, in the actual report,

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:34.100
Mueller listed ten times Trump
may have obstructed justice

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.801
and he specifically turned it
over to Congress

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:37.636
to hold Trump accountable
for those instances.

00:10:37.636 --> 00:10:40.639
And yet Graham brushed it off
saying Trump couldn't be guilty

00:10:40.639 --> 00:10:42.741
of obstruction of justice,
because it didn't work.

00:10:42.741 --> 00:10:47.579
-You have to have specific
intent to obstruct justice.

00:10:47.579 --> 00:10:51.050
If there's no underlying crime,

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:53.485
pretty hard to figure out
what intent might be

00:10:53.485 --> 00:10:57.689
if there was never a crime
to begin with.

00:10:57.689 --> 00:11:01.327
The president never did
anything to stop Mueller

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:04.730
from doing his job,
so I guess the theory goes,

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.933
now, okay, he didn't collude
with the Russians

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:11.537
and he didn't specifically
do anything to stop Mueller,

00:11:11.537 --> 00:11:14.139
but attempted obstruction
of justice of a crime

00:11:14.139 --> 00:11:17.008
that never occurred.

00:11:17.008 --> 00:11:20.346
I guess that's sort of
the new standard around here.

00:11:20.346 --> 00:11:22.848
We'll see if that
makes any sense.

00:11:22.848 --> 00:11:24.283
To me, it doesn't.

00:11:24.283 --> 00:11:26.085
&gt;&gt; Seth: Wait, so now
your argument is that

00:11:26.085 --> 00:11:28.553
attempted obstruction of justice
isn't a crime?

00:11:28.553 --> 00:11:30.055
I'm no lawyer,
but last I checked,

00:11:30.055 --> 00:11:32.758
attempting to do something
illegal is also a crime.

00:11:32.758 --> 00:11:35.694
If you get arrested for chasing
a guy down the street

00:11:35.694 --> 00:11:37.195
with a knife,
you can't go to court and say,

00:11:37.195 --> 00:11:39.131
"Sure, I tried to kill him,
but he was too fast!"

00:11:39.131 --> 00:11:40.999
[ Laughter ]

00:11:40.999 --> 00:11:43.335
Again, the report lists
ten different times Trump

00:11:43.335 --> 00:11:44.870
tried to interfere
in the investigation

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.805
or tried to get other people to
interfere in the investigation.

00:11:46.805 --> 00:11:48.340
But Graham is arguing
that because Trump

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.542
never specifically told anyone
to obstruct justice,

00:11:50.542 --> 00:11:52.611
he can't be guilty
of obstruction of justice,

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:55.213
which is a ridiculous argument.
But don't take it from me.

00:11:55.213 --> 00:11:57.549
Take it from 1999 Lindsey
Graham.

00:11:57.549 --> 00:12:00.319
-He doesn't have to say,
"go lie for me" to be a crime.

00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:02.153
You don't have to say,
"Let's obstruct justice"

00:12:02.153 --> 00:12:03.956
for it to be a crime.

00:12:03.956 --> 00:12:07.826
You judge people on their
conduct, not magic phrases.

00:12:07.826 --> 00:12:10.328
-First of all, how is it that
young Lindsey Graham

00:12:10.328 --> 00:12:12.731
looks like more of an adult
than current Lindsey Graham?

00:12:12.731 --> 00:12:14.099
[ Laughter ]

00:12:14.099 --> 00:12:15.734
Now he looks like
a 12-year-old boy

00:12:15.734 --> 00:12:18.804
who put grey dye in his hair
for a school play.

00:12:18.804 --> 00:12:21.307
20 years from now, he's just
going to be a baby in a wig.

00:12:21.307 --> 00:12:23.575
[ Laughter ]

00:12:23.575 --> 00:12:25.944
Second, what do you mean
magic phrases?

00:12:25.944 --> 00:12:28.380
What's an example
of a magic phrase?

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.382
-Trump is a [bleep] idiot.

00:12:30.382 --> 00:12:33.986
-All right. Also, Trump did...

00:12:33.986 --> 00:12:36.622
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:36.622 --> 00:12:40.825
Trump did have a specific intent
to obstruct justice.

00:12:40.825 --> 00:12:42.560
If you'd read the whole report,
you would know that.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:44.930
Because in the report, Mueller's
team specifically wrote

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:47.399
that Trump had a motive
to end the investigation,

00:12:47.399 --> 00:12:49.501
because he was afraid
they would find facts

00:12:49.501 --> 00:12:51.403
about the campaign
and the president personally

00:12:51.403 --> 00:12:53.605
that the president could have
understood to be crimes.

00:12:53.605 --> 00:12:54.773
That's why he repeatedly

00:12:54.773 --> 00:12:56.208
tried to interfere
in the investigation.

00:12:56.208 --> 00:12:57.877
For example, according
to Mueller's report,

00:12:57.877 --> 00:12:59.645
Trump told his former
White House counsel

00:12:59.645 --> 00:13:01.046
Don McGahn to fire Mueller.

00:13:01.046 --> 00:13:02.848
That anecdote is included
in Mueller's report,

00:13:02.848 --> 00:13:05.317
along with some colorful
language from McGahn.

00:13:05.317 --> 00:13:07.786
-Although McGahn recalled
receiving multiple calls

00:13:07.786 --> 00:13:09.588
from the president
on the same day,

00:13:09.588 --> 00:13:11.790
he was not certain
of the specific dates,

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:15.561
but he was confident that he had
at least two phone conversations

00:13:15.561 --> 00:13:18.930
with the president in which
the president directed him

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:21.500
to call the acting
Attorney General

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:23.501
and have the Special Counsel
removed.

00:13:23.501 --> 00:13:27.105
It's also the colorful reporting
from this report

00:13:27.105 --> 00:13:30.775
where Don McGahn says
to Reince Priebus,

00:13:30.775 --> 00:13:33.078
which is the third witness
to this incident,

00:13:33.078 --> 00:13:36.214
"The President asked me to do
some crazy [bleep]"

00:13:36.214 --> 00:13:39.251
-Man, cable news is feeling
salty today!

00:13:39.251 --> 00:13:40.319
[ Laughter ]

00:13:40.319 --> 00:13:42.021
You got Senators dropping
F-bombs,

00:13:42.021 --> 00:13:43.789
anchors saying the words
"crazy [bleep]"

00:13:43.789 --> 00:13:46.025
When Wolf Blitzer found out
about the Mueller letter,

00:13:46.025 --> 00:13:47.693
he fully went off the rails.

00:13:47.693 --> 00:13:50.329
-Alright, we got some important
breaking news --

00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:51.496
[Bleep]

00:13:51.496 --> 00:13:54.599
We got the -- [bleep]

00:13:54.599 --> 00:13:56.769
has just -- [bleep]

00:13:56.769 --> 00:13:58.370
-So we have all of this
information

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.838
from Mueller's report,
and yet instead of

00:13:59.838 --> 00:14:02.140
taking advantage of the rare
opportunity to ask

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.408
the Attorney General
of the United States

00:14:03.408 --> 00:14:04.509
about the possibility

00:14:04.509 --> 00:14:05.844
that the president
of the United States

00:14:05.844 --> 00:14:07.345
committed obstruction
of justice,

00:14:07.345 --> 00:14:10.014
Republicans chose instead
to spend most of their time

00:14:10.014 --> 00:14:12.684
obsessing over a person
who wasn't even in the room.

00:14:12.684 --> 00:14:14.653
-The Inspector General found
that during

00:14:14.653 --> 00:14:16.888
the department's investigation
of Hillary Clinton

00:14:16.888 --> 00:14:19.791
for mishandling highly
classified information,

00:14:19.791 --> 00:14:23.895
there was a culture
of unauthorized media contacts.

00:14:23.895 --> 00:14:26.564
We've heard a lot about
the Steele dossier.

00:14:26.564 --> 00:14:27.999
Mr. Steele, of course,

00:14:27.999 --> 00:14:30.269
is a former British
intelligence officer

00:14:30.269 --> 00:14:36.342
hired to do opposition research
by the Hillary Clinton campaign.

00:14:36.342 --> 00:14:39.111
-Now, he's in charge of the
Clinton e-mail investigation.

00:14:39.111 --> 00:14:40.846
-There were two investigations
here.

00:14:40.846 --> 00:14:43.381
One was an investigation
of Donald Trump.

00:14:43.381 --> 00:14:46.485
There was another investigation
of Hillary Clinton.

00:14:46.485 --> 00:14:48.186
-Oh, my God, guys, let it go.

00:14:48.186 --> 00:14:49.587
A thousand years from now

00:14:49.587 --> 00:14:51.356
when global warming
has destroyed the planet

00:14:51.356 --> 00:14:53.658
and hoards of zombie bandits
roam the countryside,

00:14:53.658 --> 00:14:55.861
a gang of survivors is going
to find an abandoned room

00:14:55.861 --> 00:14:58.563
in the Capitol with these words
scrawled in blood.

00:14:58.563 --> 00:15:00.132
"What about Hillary's e-mails?"

00:15:00.132 --> 00:15:01.866
[ Laughter ]

00:15:01.866 --> 00:15:02.935
What's clear here is that

00:15:02.935 --> 00:15:04.203
Trump's hand-picked Attorney
General

00:15:04.203 --> 00:15:06.672
orchestrated a PR Campaign
to mislead the public

00:15:06.672 --> 00:15:08.040
over Robert Mueller's findings

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:09.574
before anyone
actually got to see them.

00:15:09.574 --> 00:15:12.110
And now we know Mueller himself
was upset about it.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:13.512
If you're going to read
something,

00:15:13.512 --> 00:15:15.747
don't leave out key words.
Read the whole thing.

00:15:15.747 --> 00:15:17.182
You know, like Lindsey Graham.

00:15:17.182 --> 00:15:19.051
-Trump is a [bleep] idiot.

00:15:19.051 --> 00:15:21.320
[ Laughter ]
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.988
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:22.988 --> 00:15:25.057 line:0%
♪♪

